# Visual system

## Why the app currently looks generic

If a screen has any of the following, it is wrong. These are the specific things that make AI-built UIs look templated:

1. A card with `border` **and** `shadow-md` **and** `rounded-lg`. Three separation methods fighting.
2. Body text, labels, and headings all within 2px of each other. No hierarchy.
3. Default Tailwind `gray-*` / `slate-*`. It reads as unstyled.
4. Every element with the same padding. No density contrast between a dashboard and a table.
5. Money rendered in the body font at body size, left-aligned, in a proportional typeface.
6. Recharts left at defaults: cartesian grid, legend, tooltip box, `#8884d8`.
7. A gradient anywhere.
8. Three equal stat cards in a row across the top.

Fixing 1, 2, 5 and 6 accounts for most of the improvement.

