## Component anatomy

### Surface
One rule: `background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--hairline); border-radius: var(--r-lg);` and **no shadow**. Shadows are reserved for things that genuinely float: bottom sheets, popovers, the sticky action bar. Nothing else in the app casts a shadow.

### Figure block
```
LABEL          <- --t-micro, uppercase, tracked, --ink-faint
$4,182.55      <- --t-figure, Bricolage 600, tabular
↓ 12% vs May   <- --t-small, --ink-muted, arrow glyph carries the direction
```
Never wrap a figure block in its own card when three of them sit together. Separate with hairline dividers instead. Three bordered cards in a row is the single most recognisable generic-dashboard tell.

### Ledger row (the most-used component in the app)
```
[cat dot]  Merchant name                      −42.50
           Account · 14 Jun                   [category chip]
```
- 2 lines, 64px tall, full-bleed to the screen edge on mobile
- Category is a 8px dot in the category colour, not a coloured badge on every row
- Row separator is a hairline inset to the text start, not full width
- Date headers are sticky, `--surface-2` background, `--t-micro` uppercase
- Tap opens detail. Swipe left reveals Recategorise. Swipe right reveals Mark as transfer

### Category chip
Text at `--t-micro` in the category colour on a 12% tint of the same colour. No border. `--r-full`.

### Empty and loading states
- Loading: skeleton rows matching the real layout. Never a centred spinner.
- Empty: one line of instruction plus the action. "No transactions yet. Import a CSV to get started." with the button directly beneath.
- Error: what broke and what to do. "Row 42 has no date. Check the date column mapping." Never "Something went wrong."

