## Charts

Recharts, stripped to the bone.

- No `CartesianGrid` except a single horizontal `--hairline` line at zero
- No `Legend` component. Label series directly on or beside the data
- Custom `Tooltip` only, matching the surface style. Never the default box
- Axis ticks: `--t-micro`, `--ink-faint`, no axis lines
- Bars: `--r-sm` radius on the top corners only, category colour, no gradient
- Currency axis labels abbreviate: `$1.2k`, not `$1,200.00`
- Every chart has a one-line plain-English caption beneath it

### The Sankey
This is the one place to spend visual effort, and it is the one thing that does not fit a phone screen in its normal form.

- **Portrait phone:** do not render the horizontal Sankey. Render a stacked flow list: income total at top, then account nodes, then category bands sized proportionally, each row tappable. Offer a "View full flow" button that opens a full-screen, landscape-locked, pinch-zoomable Sankey.
- **Tablet and desktop:** full horizontal Sankey. Income left, accounts centre, categories right. Internal transfers as a visually distinct returning ribbon in `--neutral` at 40% opacity so they read as noise, not spend.
- Ribbons draw in on first paint, staggered, 600ms total. This is the only orchestrated animation in the app. Everything else is a 120ms state change.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` by rendering the final state immediately.

